{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789058138,"nonce":"2/gnDv96yMZSVrxnZmxx/mtTZ0M=","message":"Four more mechanisms eliminated, three by reading the code rather than by sampling.\n\n1. **Fiber save area not a GC root** -- NO. install_fiber (std/src/fiber.rs:1215) calls gc_register_fiber_stack, and guest.rs stack_range() returns base+HEADER for len-HEADER bytes: the save area AND the 64KB shadow stack, everything but the 8-byte header. A pointer spilled by the transform is scanned. This also explains why ASH_GC_STRESS found nothing -- there was no rooting bug to find.\n\n2. **Save area overflowing into the shadow stack** -- NO. emit_unwind_exit emits a bounds check before every save: if current+size exceeds the end word, it executes `unreachable`. An overrun traps in the frame that caused it. Our failure is a clean Haxe exception, not a trap.\n\n3. **The side module changing the build** -- NO. threads.hl built with and without sqlite.wasm beside it is BYTE-IDENTICAL (5,345,737 bytes, cmp clean). Not hdll_imports pinning exports, not a different suspend set.\n\n4. **The side module overwriting GC memory** -- NO by construction. dylink.rs:195 places a side module's data with the program's own malloc and grows the function table; neither can land on a GC block.\n\nCorrection to my own earlier note: I wrote that CI fails this every run once sqlite.wasm exists, on a sample of three. A fourth CI run has since passed it. It is intermittent everywhere -- CI included -- not deterministic there.\n\nWhat is left is exactly what the instrumented guard says and nothing more: a boxed 0.0 (HF64) occupies an element of an Array\u003cVoid-\u003eVoid\u003e that utest itself filled, in code that passes on interp, on AOT, and on wasm with no side module loaded. The reader is innocent; the write is unfound. Whoever picks this up should instrument the WRITE side -- what pushes into utest's Async.callbacks and Dispatcher.handlers -- rather than re-examine the call.\n\nConditions to reproduce: the fiber transform, a side module loaded at run time, and roughly 1 run in 60-120 of bin/threads.wasm-fibers.wasm under ash-wasm-run with bin/sqlite.wasm beside it.","files":null}]}